# Normalise text; declare binaries explicitly.
#
# git decides "binary" by looking for a NUL byte in roughly the first 8KB.  Any format
# whose header is plain ASCII can be misdetected as text, and with core.autocrlf=true
# (the normal Windows setup here) every LF in it is then expanded to CRLF on clone --
# silently corrupting the file.  Declaring the extension is the only reliable fix, so a
# new binary artifact type gets an entry here BEFORE it is first committed.
#
# Verify a new type with a throwaway `git clone . <tmp>` and by LOADING the cloned file
# the way the code loads it -- not by comparing sizes, and not by opening it in a viewer.

* text=auto

*.parquet binary
*.zst     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.ico     binary
*.zip     binary
*.pem     binary
